BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bigci-environmental-awards-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260926T162453Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260802
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260803
SUMMARY:Deadline: BigCi Environmental Awards 2026
DESCRIPTION:BigCi's Environmental Awards are an annual prize for work that 
 engages with the environment\, open to Australian and international artist
 s working in visual art\, installation\, multimedia\, performance\, litera
 ture\, music\, photography\, filmmaking and curating. TWO WINNERS each rec
 eive four weeks of free residency at BigCi plus AUD 5\,000 in prize money.
  BigCi sits on the edge of Wollemi National Park in the Greater Blue Mount
 ains\, an hour and a half from Sydney but geologically another world\; win
 ners explore the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Wollemi\, Blue Mountains and
  Gardens of Stone National Parks on guided walks and are given research as
 sistance relevant to their projects. At the end of their residencies they 
 present the work at the BigCi Open Day. JUDGING: three independent judges\
 , Lea Kannar-Lichtenberger (Australia)\, Brian Wallace (China) and Dan Got
 tlieb (USA). APPLICATION: an online submission form (Wufoo) linked from th
 e awards page\, with a non-refundable AUD 40 entry fee paid at the time of
  submission. KEY DATES: submissions close 2 August 2026\; winners announce
 d 22 August 2026. Enquiries via the contact form at bigci.org/contact.\n\n
 Organisation: Bilpin International Ground for Creative Initiatives (BigCi)
 \nLocation: Bilpin\, New South Wales\, Australia\, on the edge of Wollemi 
 National Park in the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Greater Blue Mountains\,
  about 1.5 hours from Sydney. Open to Australian and international artists
 .\nAward: Two awards\, each of AUD 5\,000 prize money plus four weeks of f
 ree residency at BigCi\, guided walks in the surrounding national parks an
 d research assistance for the project. AUD 40 entry fee\, non-refundable a
 nd payable with the submission.\nDuration: Four-week residency at BigCi pe
 r winner\n\nMore: https://bigci.org/awards/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://bigci.org/awards/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_med
 ium=referral
LOCATION:Bilpin\, New South Wales\, Australia\, on the edge of Wollemi Nati
 onal Park in the UNESCO World Heritage-listed Greater Blue Mountains\, abo
 ut 1.5 hours from Sydney. Open to Australian and international artists.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:creative-australia-arts-projects-organisations-2026@artificialnouveau.g
 ithub.io
DTSTAMP:20260926T162453Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Deadline: Creative Australia: Arts Projects for Organisations (Sept
 ember 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:Creative Australia's principal open-round project grant for art
 s organisations and the most directly relevant Australian scheme for mount
 ing festivals\, exhibitions and public programmes. The guidelines explicit
 ly list festivals\, productions\, exhibitions\, performances\, touring\, p
 ublishing\, recording\, collaborations\, research and community engagement
  as supported activity. Organisations may propose either a single project 
 or an entire programme of projects\, which can extend to a full artistic p
 rogramme for a given calendar year or longer\, so this can function as de 
 facto annual programme funding. The category is artform-agnostic and routi
 nely supports media arts\, digital culture\, experimental sound and art-an
 d-science work\; activity delivered online is explicitly permitted. NOTABL
 E: international organisations are eligible where the project demonstrably
  benefits practising Australian artists\, their work\, or Australian audie
 nces\, so a non-Australian festival can apply if it is programming Austral
 ian artists. The applicant must be a legally constituted entity: incorpora
 ted association\, company limited by guarantee\, or government statutory a
 uthority. Registration in the Application Management System must be comple
 ted at least one business day before the closing date. The round closes 1 
 September 2026 at 3pm AEST.\n\nOrganisation: Creative Australia\nLocation:
  Activity may take place nationally within Australia\, internationally\, o
 r online.\nAward: AUD 20\,000 to 100\,000. No matching or co-financing req
 uirement. No application fee. Organisational administrative costs should g
 enerally not exceed 10 percent of the total project budget or the applicat
 ion becomes less competitive.\nDuration: Activity must last no longer than
  two years from the proposed start date\; the project must commence after 
 notification and within one year of it.\n\nMore: https://creative.gov.au/i
 nvestments-opportunities/arts-projects-organisations?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://creative.gov.au/investments-opportunities/arts-projects-organis
 ations?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Activity may take place nationally within Australia\, internationa
 lly\, or online.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:melbourne-queer-film-festival-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260926T162453Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:Deadline: Melbourne Queer Film Festival 2026 Submissions
DESCRIPTION:MQFF\, Australia's largest queer film festival\, accepts intern
 ational films of interest to LGBTQIA+ audiences. Deadline 3 August 2026\; 
 fees USD 30 for shorts and USD 50 for features\, with fee waivers reserved
  for Australian and First Nations entrants.\n\nOrganisation: Melbourne Que
 er Film Festival (MQFF)\nLocation: Melbourne\, Australia (festival 12-22 N
 ovember 2026). Open internationally.\nAward: Screening at Australia's larg
 est queer film festival. Fees USD 30 shorts / USD 50 features (waivers for
  Australian and First Nations entrants only).\nDuration: Festival 12-22 No
 vember 2026.\n\nMore: https://filmfreeway.com/MelbourneQueerFilmFestival?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://filmfreeway.com/MelbourneQueerFilmFestival?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Melbourne\, Australia (festival 12-22 November 2026). Open interna
 tionally.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:helpmann-fellowships-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260926T162453Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260831
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260901
SUMMARY:Deadline: Helpmann Fellowships 2026
DESCRIPTION:Three Helpmann Fellowships of up to AUD 7\,500 support ambitiou
 s\, self-directed projects that advance the artistic and professional deve
 lopment of emerging creatives. Fellowships are open across all eligible di
 sciplines\, to individuals and to collectives\, and funding can go to larg
 er-scale creative projects\, tailored professional development\, or a comb
 ination of both. Previous fellowships have supported the creation of new w
 ork\, exhibitions and performances\, residencies and internships\, touring
  and recording\, specialised training\, and long-term professional develop
 ment\; each fellowship is shaped by the recipient rather than a fixed prog
 ramme. ELIGIBILITY IS NARROW AND GEOGRAPHIC: applicants must be current re
 sidents of South Australia and either final-year students or graduates wit
 hin five years of a supported degree at Adelaide University\, the Universi
 ty of Adelaide\, Flinders University\, or the University of South Australi
 a. Honours students and graduates (up to five years after the final year o
 f study) are eligible where honours was undertaken directly following the 
 undergraduate degree. Masters and PhD candidates and graduates are not eli
 gible unless they qualify through their undergraduate or honours study. Fi
 nal-year students may apply provided the funded activity takes place after
  studies are completed and within the activity timeframe. Applications are
  assessed on artistic merit\, alignment with career development\, feasibil
 ity\, commitment to learning\, and level of ambition. The online applicati
 on requires a CV (max two pages)\, an official academic transcript\, a bud
 get on the Helpmann template\, a timeline\, project confirmations\, letter
 s of support from an academic and an industry referee\, and four to six im
 ages or one to two audio-visual work samples. An online information sessio
 n runs 4 August 2026 at 6pm ACST\, and the Program Manager\, Toni Wills\, 
 takes online or in-person application chats (info@helpmannacademy.com.au).
  Applications opened 15 July 2026 and close 31 August 2026 at 11:59pm ACST
 \, for activity occurring 1 January to 31 December 2027. Free to apply.\n\
 nOrganisation: Helpmann Academy\nLocation: South Australia (applicant must
  be a current South Australian resident)\; funded activity may take place 
 anywhere.\nAward: Up to AUD 7\,500 per fellowship\, three fellowships avai
 lable. Supported by the James & Diana Ramsay Foundation. No application fe
 e.\nDuration: Funded activity must occur between 1 January 2027 and 31 Dec
 ember 2027\n\nMore: https://helpmannacademy.com.au/helpmann-fellowships/?u
 tm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://helpmannacademy.com.au/helpmann-fellowships/?utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:South Australia (applicant must be a current South Australian resi
 dent)\; funded activity may take place anywhere.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-global-fellowships-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260926T162453Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270211
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270212
SUMMARY:Deadline: Screen Australia Global Fellowships (AUD 80\,000-100\,000
 )
DESCRIPTION:Screen Australia's Global Fellowships support Australian screen
  practitioners (producers\, directors\, writers and development executives
 ) pursuing international professional development and career acceleration 
 through placements with leading global screen organizations. SUPPORT: up t
 o 10 fellows annually\, each receiving a non-recoupable grant of AUD 80\,0
 00 for a single continuous placement of up to 6 months\, or AUD 100\,000 f
 or multiple placements over up to 12 months\, plus up to AUD 5\,000 for ca
 rers' and/or accessibility costs. ELIGIBILITY: Australian citizens or perm
 anent residents (sole traders) or incorporated Australian companies with a
 n ABN\; applicants must secure their own fellowship opportunity with host 
 organizations and mentors (Screen Australia does not broker placements) an
 d be eligible for required visas. ASSESSMENT: track record and professiona
 l achievement\, quality of the fellowship opportunity\, career impact\, an
 d anticipated benefit to Australia's screen sector\, weighted equally. HOW
  TO APPLY: one application per deadline via Screen Australia's funding por
 tal. Notification 2 April 2027. DEADLINE: 11 February 2027 at 5pm AEST.\n\
 nOrganisation: Screen Australia\nLocation: International placements with l
 eading global screen organizations\, self-arranged by the fellow. Open to 
 Australian citizens or permanent residents (sole traders) or incorporated 
 Australian companies.\nAward: Non-recoupable grants of AUD 80\,000 (single
  continuous placement of up to 6 months) or AUD 100\,000 (multiple placeme
 nts over up to 12 months)\, plus up to AUD 5\,000 for carers' and/or acces
 sibility costs. Up to 10 fellows annually.\nDuration: Placements of up to 
 6 months (single) or up to 12 months (multiple)\n\nMore: https://www.scree
 naustralia.gov.au/fund/global-fellowships/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/global-fellowships/?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:International placements with leading global screen organizations\
 , self-arranged by the fellow. Open to Australian citizens or permanent re
 sidents (sole traders) or incorporated Australian companies.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-first-nations-feature-development-2026@artificialnouve
 au.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260926T162453Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:Deadline: Screen Australia First Nations Feature Development (up to
  AUD 45\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Screen Australia's First Nations Department funds the developme
 nt of feature film screenplays by Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander fi
 lmmakers: a first or subsequent draft feature screenplay\, including\, whe
 re appropriate\, fees for writer\, producer\, director and story consultan
 t. SUPPORT: up to AUD 30\,000\, or up to AUD 45\,000 with a producer attac
 hed. ELIGIBILITY: applicants must be a producer\, writer or writer/directo
 r who is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander Australian with at least 
 three eligible drama credits in their role. In co-writing teams mixing Fir
 st Nations and non-Indigenous writers\, the original concept must originat
 e from the First Nations writer. Writers and writer-directors are limited 
 to two development tranches as solo applicants without a producer\; attach
 ed producers must be experienced\, have two or more eligible drama credits
 \, or be emerging producers partnered with an experienced producer. Screen
  Australia may require a story consultant attachment. HOW TO APPLY: via th
 e SmartyGrants application portal\; decisions take about six weeks from th
 e deadline. DEADLINE: 22 October 2026 at 5pm AEST\, with subsequent rounds
  closing 14 January\, 11 March and 6 May 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Screen Aus
 tralia\nLocation: Australia. Open to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander
  producers\, writers and writer/directors.\nAward: Up to AUD 30\,000\, or 
 up to AUD 45\,000 with a producer attached\, covering screenplay developme
 nt including fees for writer\, producer\, director and story consultant wh
 ere appropriate.\n\nMore: https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/first-na
 tions-feature-development/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_mediu
 m=referral
URL:https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/first-nations-feature-developme
 nt/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia. Open to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander producers
 \, writers and writer/directors.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-first-nations-tv-drama-development-2026@artificialnouv
 eau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260926T162453Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:Deadline: Screen Australia First Nations TV Drama Development (up t
 o AUD 65\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Screen Australia's First Nations Department funds the developme
 nt of TV drama projects by Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander practitio
 ners: written and visual materials including treatments\, scripts\, series
  bibles\, research and production financing strategies for telemovies or T
 V drama series. SUPPORT: up to AUD 30\,000 for one-offs (AUD 45\,000 with 
 a producer attached) and up to AUD 65\,000 for series\, other than in exce
 ptional circumstances\; funding is provided as a grant. ELIGIBILITY: appli
 cants must be a producer\, writer or writer/director who is an Aboriginal 
 or Torres Strait Islander practitioner with at least two eligible drama cr
 edits in their role. In co-writing teams mixing First Nations and non-Indi
 genous writers\, the original concept must originate from the First Nation
 s writer. Writers and writer-directors may receive at most two funding tra
 nches as solo applicants without a producer\; producers must be experience
 d\, have two eligible drama credits\, or be emerging producers working wit
 h an experienced producer. Assessment weighs concept strength\, storytelli
 ng quality\, development strategy\, team experience and project viability.
  NOTE: if the project is later produced without Screen Australia productio
 n funding\, development money may need to be repaid to acquire copyright i
 nterests. HOW TO APPLY: via the SmartyGrants application portal\; decision
 s take about six weeks. DEADLINE: 22 October 2026 at 5pm AEST\, with subse
 quent rounds in January\, March and May 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Screen Aust
 ralia\nLocation: Australia. Open to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander 
 producers\, writers and writer/directors.\nAward: Up to AUD 30\,000 for on
 e-off projects (AUD 45\,000 with a producer attached) and up to AUD 65\,00
 0 for series\, other than in exceptional circumstances. Provided as a gran
 t.\n\nMore: https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/first-nations-tv-drama
 -development/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/first-nations-tv-drama-developm
 ent/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia. Open to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander producers
 \, writers and writer/directors.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:screen-australia-first-nations-documentary-development-2026@artificialn
 ouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260926T162453Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
SUMMARY:Deadline: Screen Australia First Nations Documentary Development (u
 p to AUD 30\,000)
DESCRIPTION:Screen Australia's First Nations Department funds documentary d
 evelopment by Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander key creatives: written
  and visual materials\, treatments\, draft scripts\, series bibles\, resea
 rch\, and fees for writers\, producers\, directors and story consultants. 
 SUPPORT: up to AUD 30\,000 for feature and series documentaries intended f
 or commissioning platforms\, and up to AUD 20\,000 for one-hour television
  documentaries and online series. ELIGIBILITY: sole applicants must be Aus
 tralian Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander key creatives (writer\, produ
 cer or director)\; writers/directors need at least one eligible documentar
 y credit\; producers must be experienced\, have two eligible documentary c
 redits\, or be emerging producers applying with an experienced mentor. In 
 teams\, directors and co-directors must be First Nations Australian\, and 
 in mixed co-writing teams the original concept must originate from the Fir
 st Nations writer. Projects must be documentaries under ACMA standards (no
  reality TV\, entertainment\, current affairs or educational-focused produ
 ctions). NOTE: projects receiving over AUD 50\,000 in combined development
  funds require a solicitor's opinion letter on chain of title. HOW TO APPL
 Y: via the SmartyGrants application portal\; decisions take about six week
 s. DEADLINE: 22 October 2026 at 5pm AEST\, with subsequent rounds in Janua
 ry\, March and May 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Screen Australia\nLocation: Aust
 ralia. Open to Australian Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander key creati
 ves (writer\, producer or director).\nAward: Up to AUD 30\,000 for feature
  and series documentaries intended for commissioning platforms\; up to AUD
  20\,000 for one-hour television documentaries and for online series. Prov
 ided as a grant.\n\nMore: https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/first-na
 tions-documentary-development/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_m
 edium=referral
URL:https://www.screenaustralia.gov.au/fund/first-nations-documentary-devel
 opment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Australia. Open to Australian Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islande
 r key creatives (writer\, producer or director).
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
